@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+# Design — The Through-Line
+
+## Direction
+
+Use a restrained editorial system: deep navy ground, white content cards, blue structure, and a gold through-line that advances from established experience toward a clearly named next role. The line is the visual metaphor and remains purposeful rather than decorative.
+
+## Type and color
+
+Use Proxima Nova with the provided fallback. Headlines are 72–96px, body copy is at least 40px, and compact labels are at least 22px. Use only the supplied navy, paper, blue, gold, muted, and subtle-fill tokens.
+
+## Layout
+
+Keep content inside 120px frame padding and above the reserved footer. Each beat has one dominant idea. Case studies pair a person label with proof and a future-facing role. Framework beats use numbered nodes connected by the through-line.
+
+## Motion
+
+One paused, seekable timeline controls all motion. Each clip enters in 0.5 seconds, holds for reading, and exits in 0.3 seconds. The through-line draws forward as each idea arrives. No infinite motion or autonomous playback.
