+<!doctype html>
+<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
+<title>How to Reposition Your Career</title>
+<style>
+:root{--navy:#0d2437;--deep:#0a1e2f;--blue:#3393d6;--gold:#eaab2d;--paper:#fff;--subtle:#e5eff6;--muted:#98a4cc}
+*{box-sizing:border-box} html,body{margin:0;width:100%;height:100%;overflow:hidden;background:var(--deep);font-family:"proxima-nova","Proxima Nova",system-ui,sans-serif}
+#composition{position:relative;width:1920px;height:1080px;background:var(--navy);color:var(--paper);overflow:hidden}
+#composition:before{content:"";position:absolute;inset:0;background:radial-gradient(circle at 82% 16%,rgba(51,147,214,.18),transparent 34%);pointer-events:none}
+.brand{position:absolute;left:120px;top:55px;font-weight:900;font-size:24px;letter-spacing:.12em;color:var(--gold)}
+.brand em{font-style:normal;color:var(--paper)}
+.clip{position:absolute;inset:130px 120px 120px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;opacity:0;visibility:hidden;transform:translateY(22px)}
+.eyebrow{font-size:22px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.15em;color:var(--blue);margin-bottom:24px} .eyebrow span{color:var(--gold);margin-left:18px}
+.rule{width:150px;height:4px;background:var(--gold);margin-bottom:32px;transform-origin:left}
+h1{font-size:84px;line-height:.98;letter-spacing:-.025em;max-width:1450px;margin:0 0 35px;font-weight:900}
+.narration{font-size:40px;line-height:1.25;max-width:1580px;margin:0;color:#f6f6f9}
+.case h1{color:var(--gold)} .step h1{font-size:76px;color:var(--paper)}
+.through-line{position:absolute;left:0;right:0;bottom:5px;height:10px;background:rgba(51,147,214,.22);border-radius:10px;overflow:visible}
+.through-line i{display:block;width:100%;height:4px;margin-top:3px;background:var(--blue);transform-origin:left}
+.through-line b{position:absolute;right:-2px;top:-7px;width:24px;height:24px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--gold)}
+.footer{position:absolute;right:120px;bottom:55px;font-size:22px;font-weight:700;color:var(--muted)}
+</style></head>
+<body><main id="composition" data-composition-id="m3_how-to-reposition-your-career" data-start="0" data-duration="228.86" data-fps="30" data-width="1920" data-height="1080">
+<div class="brand">SCLA <em>CAREER DEVELOPMENT</em></div>
+<section class="clip core" id="beat-01" data-clip-id="beat-01" data-beat-id="beat-01" data-start="0.0" data-end="8.7" data-duration="8.7" data-track-index="1"" aria-label="A Pivot Isn&#x27;t a Reset">
+      <div class="eyebrow">MID-CAREER MOMENTUM <span>01</span></div>
+      <div class="rule"></div>
+      <h1>A Pivot Isn&#x27;t a Reset</h1>
+      <p class="narration">When people hear &quot;career pivot&quot; or &quot;repositioning,&quot; they picture starting completely over. New degree, new industry, and new identity.</p>
+      <div class="through-line"><i></i><b></b></div>
+    </section><section class="clip core" id="beat-02" data-clip-id="beat-02" data-beat-id="beat-02" data-start="8.7" data-end="21.51" data-duration="12.81" data-track-index="1"" aria-label="Re-Tell What You Already Have">
+      <div class="eyebrow">MID-CAREER MOMENTUM <span>02</span></div>
+      <div class="rule"></div>
+      <h1>Re-Tell What You Already Have</h1>
+      <p class="narration">In reality, most successful pivots are strategic repositionings of the experience you already have. You&#x27;re not erasing your past; you&#x27;re re-telling it so it clearly points to the future you want.</p>
+      <div class="through-line"><i></i><b></b></div>
+    </section><section class="clip core" id="beat-03" data-clip-id="beat-03" data-beat-id="beat-03" data-start="21.51" data-end="26.66" data-duration="5.15" data-track-index="1"" aria-label="Three Professionals · One Pattern">
+      <div class="eyebrow">MID-CAREER MOMENTUM <span>03</span></div>
+      <div class="rule"></div>
+      <h1>Three Professionals · One Pattern</h1>
+      <p class="narration">Let&#x27;s look at how three mid-career professionals did exactly that.</p>
+      <div class="through-line"><i></i><b></b></div>
+    </section><section class="clip case" id="beat-04" data-clip-id="beat-04" data-beat-id="beat-04" data-start="26.66" data-end="42.21" data-duration="15.55" data-track-index="1"" aria-label="Alex: Operations → Strategy">
+      <div class="eyebrow">MID-CAREER MOMENTUM <span>04</span></div>
+      <div class="rule"></div>
+      <h1>Alex: Operations → Strategy</h1>
+      <p class="narration">Alex spent ten years as an Operations Manager—keeping processes smooth, teams on their numbers, and projects on track. On paper, the roles looked operational — not strategic. But Alex had led cross-functional projects, redesigned systems, and shaped decisions.</p>
+      <div class="through-line"><i></i><b></b></div>
+    </section><section class="clip case" id="beat-05" data-clip-id="beat-05" data-beat-id="beat-05" data-start="42.21" data-end="76.19" data-duration="33.98" data-track-index="1"" aria-label="Surface the Strategic Work">
+      <div class="eyebrow">MID-CAREER MOMENTUM <span>05</span></div>
+      <div class="rule"></div>
+      <h1>Surface the Strategic Work</h1>
+      <p class="narration">To reposition for a Strategy Leader role, Alex did three things. Curated experiences that showed strategic thinking—like redesigning a workflow that saved time and money. Rewrote bullets to emphasize decisions, outcomes, and scope—turning &quot;managed operations&quot; into &quot;Led a multi-department initiative that reduced processing time by 25% and improved customer satisfaction.&quot; And updated LinkedIn to point forward: &quot;Operations &amp; Strategy Leader.&quot; Alex didn&#x27;t claim a title that wasn&#x27;t earned—just surfaced the strategic work already inside those operations roles, and started applying with that focus.</p>
+      <div class="through-line"><i></i><b></b></div>
+    </section><section class="clip case" id="beat-06" data-clip-id="beat-06" data-beat-id="beat-06" data-start="76.19" data-end="89.39" data-duration="13.2" data-track-index="1"" aria-label="Jordan: Teaching → Learning Design">
+      <div class="eyebrow">MID-CAREER MOMENTUM <span>06</span></div>
+      <div class="rule"></div>
+      <h1>Jordan: Teaching → Learning Design</h1>
+      <p class="narration">Jordan spent years teaching—designing lessons, assessments, and learning experiences—and wanted to move into instructional design and learning technologies, a field that often uses different language and sits in different departments.</p>
+      <div class="through-line"><i></i><b></b></div>
+    </section><section class="clip case" id="beat-07" data-clip-id="beat-07" data-beat-id="beat-07" data-start="89.39" data-end="113.57" data-duration="24.18" data-track-index="1"" aria-label="Translate into Design Language">
+      <div class="eyebrow">MID-CAREER MOMENTUM <span>07</span></div>
+      <div class="rule"></div>
+      <h1>Translate into Design Language</h1>
+      <p class="narration">So Jordan translated teaching tasks into design language: &quot;Designed and implemented multi-modal learning experiences for diverse learners.&quot; Jordan highlighted the tools and methods used—learning platforms, data analysis, collaborative project design—and updated that LinkedIn headline to &quot;Learning Experience Designer.&quot; The classroom didn&#x27;t disappear. It became proof of strong design, facilitation, and learner-centered thinking—directly relevant to the new field.</p>
+      <div class="through-line"><i></i><b></b></div>
+    </section><section class="clip case" id="beat-08" data-clip-id="beat-08" data-beat-id="beat-08" data-start="113.57" data-end="124.03" data-duration="10.46" data-track-index="1"" aria-label="Priya: Contributor → People Leader">
+      <div class="eyebrow">MID-CAREER MOMENTUM <span>08</span></div>
+      <div class="rule"></div>
+      <h1>Priya: Contributor → People Leader</h1>
+      <p class="narration">Priya built her career as a strong individual contributor—owning complex work, building relationships, delivering results—and wanted to step into a first-line leadership role.</p>
+      <div class="through-line"><i></i><b></b></div>
+    </section><section class="clip case" id="beat-09" data-clip-id="beat-09" data-beat-id="beat-09" data-start="124.03" data-end="145.85" data-duration="21.82" data-track-index="1"" aria-label="Name the Leadership Already Happening">
+      <div class="eyebrow">MID-CAREER MOMENTUM <span>09</span></div>
+      <div class="rule"></div>
+      <h1>Name the Leadership Already Happening</h1>
+      <p class="narration">She found the moments she&#x27;d already led informally—coordinating project teams, mentoring colleagues, onboarding new hires. And rewrote her bullets to show it: &quot;Mentored 3 new analysts, accelerating their ramp-up time by 30%.&quot; Her summary became &quot;Emerging people leader with a track record of mentoring, coordinating cross-team projects, and growing others while delivering results.&quot;</p>
+      <div class="through-line"><i></i><b></b></div>
+    </section><section class="clip core" id="beat-10" data-clip-id="beat-10" data-beat-id="beat-10" data-start="145.85" data-end="151.0" data-duration="5.15" data-track-index="1"" aria-label="The Shared Pattern">
+      <div class="eyebrow">MID-CAREER MOMENTUM <span>10</span></div>
+      <div class="rule"></div>
+      <h1>The Shared Pattern</h1>
+      <p class="narration">Across all three, the pattern is the same.</p>
+      <div class="through-line"><i></i><b></b></div>
+    </section><section class="clip step" id="beat-11" data-clip-id="beat-11" data-beat-id="beat-11" data-start="151.0" data-end="163.81" data-duration="12.81" data-track-index="1"" aria-label="1 · Clarify Your Direction">
+      <div class="eyebrow">MID-CAREER MOMENTUM <span>11</span></div>
+      <div class="rule"></div>
+      <h1>1 · Clarify Your Direction</h1>
+      <p class="narration">Clarify your future direction. Know whether you&#x27;re aiming for a promotion, a lateral move, or a role redesign—and what kinds of roles you want to show up on your radar.</p>
+      <div class="through-line"><i></i><b></b></div>
+    </section><section class="clip step" id="beat-12" data-clip-id="beat-12" data-beat-id="beat-12" data-start="163.81" data-end="174.26" data-duration="10.45" data-track-index="1"" aria-label="2 · Curate Your Story">
+      <div class="eyebrow">MID-CAREER MOMENTUM <span>12</span></div>
+      <div class="rule"></div>
+      <h1>2 · Curate Your Story</h1>
+      <p class="narration">Curate your story. Select the experiences that clearly connect your present to that future—projects, responsibilities, and results that already demonstrate the skills you&#x27;ll need.</p>
+      <div class="through-line"><i></i><b></b></div>
+    </section><section class="clip step" id="beat-13" data-clip-id="beat-13" data-beat-id="beat-13" data-start="174.26" data-end="184.32" data-duration="10.06" data-track-index="1"" aria-label="3 · Translate Your Language">
+      <div class="eyebrow">MID-CAREER MOMENTUM <span>13</span></div>
+      <div class="rule"></div>
+      <h1>3 · Translate Your Language</h1>
+      <p class="narration">Translate your language. Rewrite bullets and profile sections in the words of your target roles—strategy, design, leadership, analytics, systems, whatever fits your path.</p>
+      <div class="through-line"><i></i><b></b></div>
+    </section><section class="clip step" id="beat-14" data-clip-id="beat-14" data-beat-id="beat-14" data-start="184.32" data-end="192.82" data-duration="8.5" data-track-index="1"" aria-label="4 · Update Public Signals">
+      <div class="eyebrow">MID-CAREER MOMENTUM <span>14</span></div>
+      <div class="rule"></div>
+      <h1>4 · Update Public Signals</h1>
+      <p class="narration">Update your public signals. Align your resume, LinkedIn headline, summary, and even your 60-second career story with that future-focused positioning.</p>
+      <div class="through-line"><i></i><b></b></div>
+    </section><section class="clip core" id="beat-15" data-clip-id="beat-15" data-beat-id="beat-15" data-start="192.82" data-end="207.19" data-duration="14.37" data-track-index="1"" aria-label="Reveal the Through-Line">
+      <div class="eyebrow">MID-CAREER MOMENTUM <span>15</span></div>
+      <div class="rule"></div>
+      <h1>Reveal the Through-Line</h1>
+      <p class="narration">Repositioning your career isn&#x27;t about being someone you&#x27;re not. It&#x27;s about revealing the through-line in what you&#x27;ve already done—and telling that story in a way that makes your next move feel obvious to others.</p>
+      <div class="through-line"><i></i><b></b></div>
+    </section><section class="clip core" id="beat-16" data-clip-id="beat-16" data-beat-id="beat-16" data-start="207.19" data-end="219.22" data-duration="12.03" data-track-index="1"" aria-label="Point Experience Toward What’s Next">
+      <div class="eyebrow">MID-CAREER MOMENTUM <span>16</span></div>
+      <div class="rule"></div>
+      <h1>Point Experience Toward What’s Next</h1>
+      <p class="narration">As you move forward in this track, keep asking: how can I tell the true story of my experience so it clearly points to the roles I want next?</p>
+      <div class="through-line"><i></i><b></b></div>
+    </section><section class="clip core" id="beat-17" data-clip-id="beat-17" data-beat-id="beat-17" data-start="219.22" data-end="228.86" data-duration="9.64" data-track-index="1"" aria-label="Open New Doors—without Starting Over">
+      <div class="eyebrow">MID-CAREER MOMENTUM <span>17</span></div>
+      <div class="rule"></div>
+      <h1>Open New Doors—without Starting Over</h1>
+      <p class="narration">That&#x27;s the heart of repositioning—and one of the most powerful ways to open new doors without starting from scratch.</p>
+      <div class="through-line"><i></i><b></b></div>
+    </section>
+<div class="footer">How to Reposition Your Career</div>
+</main>
